WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.584 --> 00:00:16.169
the days passed, Tommy and Jack began to admire Dan because he was courageous.

2
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:22.034
Demi, who loved to read, regarded Dan as a walking storybook.

3
00:00:23.536 --> 00:00:27.839
That was because Dan could describe his adventures in a most exciting way.

4
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.483
It pleased Dan that the boys liked him, so he made an effort to be friendly.

5
00:00:36.045 --> 00:00:41.949
But he felt that Jo and the professor didn't trust him, so he took delight in trying their

6
00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:45.551
patience. One of Mr.

7
00:00:45.571 --> 00:00:48.493
Bauer's strictest rules was no fighting.

8
00:00:48.513 --> 00:00:52.976
"You should never fight," he reminded the boys one day.

9
00:00:52.997 --> 00:00:57.620
"It's not an effective way to settle a dispute or entertain others."

10
00:00:59.244 --> 00:01:00.365
"What a stupid rule!"

11
00:01:00.685 --> 00:01:02.147
Dan said under his breath.

12
00:01:04.529 --> 00:01:09.933
Later that afternoon the boys were bored and looking for something interesting to do.

13
00:01:09.953 --> 00:01:14.757
"Tell us another story about a fight you won," Demi said.

14
00:01:14.777 --> 00:01:21.503
"Never mind that," Tommy said, "I'd like to learn how to box!"

15
00:01:22.624 --> 00:01:25.366
"I'll teach you, but do you promise not to tell Mr.

16
00:01:25.406 --> 00:01:26.888
Bauer?" Dan asked.

17
00:01:28.524 --> 00:01:29.305
"Oh, yes!"

18
00:01:29.725 --> 00:01:31.026
they all cried at once.

19
00:01:32.266 --> 00:01:37.349
The boys went behind the barn, where Dan proceeded to give them boxing lessons.

20
00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:45.094
That was enough to satisfy Demi, Tommy, and Nat, but Jack wanted a real fight.

21
00:01:45.114 --> 00:01:46.935
"Come on!"

22
00:01:47.255 --> 00:01:48.716
Jack challenged Dan.

23
00:01:48.736 --> 00:01:51.437
"I bet I could beat you!"

24
00:01:51.457 --> 00:01:56.140
"Yeah," Tommy shouted, "let's see a fight!"

25
00:01:58.316 --> 00:02:01.358
Dan pulled off his jacket, and the match began.

26
00:02:02.719 --> 00:02:05.980
But just as the boys started punching each other, Mr.

27
00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.581
Bauer rushed toward them.

28
00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:10.143
"Stop this at once!"

29
00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:12.964
he roared, separating the two fighters.

30
00:02:12.984 --> 00:02:15.946
"You should be ashamed of yourselves!"

31
00:02:17.427 --> 00:02:18.007
"Let me go!"

32
00:02:19.008 --> 00:02:19.788
Dan shouted.

33
00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:26.812
His shirt was torn, and his eye was beginning to swell shut.

34
00:02:28.664 --> 00:02:31.725
Jack's chin was covered with blood from a cut lip.

35
00:02:31.745 --> 00:02:36.086
"You know fighting's forbidden here, right?"

36
00:02:36.446 --> 00:02:39.407
Mr. Bauer asked Dan in his angriest voice.

37
00:02:39.427 --> 00:02:42.308
"Yes," Dan growled.

38
00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:45.129
"Then why did you break the rule?"

39
00:02:45.149 --> 00:02:48.630
"Every fellow needs to learn to defend himself."

40
00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:53.231
"These boys will do fine without learning how to injure each other.

41
00:02:54.451 --> 00:02:59.545
Now go wash up, Jack and Dan, and remember, Dan, if you break any more rules, you'll be

42
00:02:59.585 --> 00:03:00.166
sent away."

43
00:03:01.527 --> 00:03:06.730
But that warning only served as a challenge to Dan, who was soon in trouble again.

44
00:03:08.171 --> 00:03:11.653
A week later the boys were out making fishing poles from sticks.

45
00:03:14.015 --> 00:03:19.278
On the way home, Tommy was riding the donkey, Toby, and carrying his new pole.

46
00:03:19.298 --> 00:03:26.843
"You look just like a bullfighter, Tommy," Demi said, thinking of a picture in one of his favorite

47
00:03:26.884 --> 00:03:33.515
books. "Only you're not wearing fancy clothes or carrying a red cloth."

48
00:03:33.535 --> 00:03:36.377
"Let's have a bullfight!"

49
00:03:36.717 --> 00:03:39.820
Dan said, intent on making mischief.

50
00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:44.763
"Ride at that old cow over there in the meadow—let's see her run."

51
00:03:44.783 --> 00:03:47.785
"Don't annoy Buttercup!"

52
00:03:48.185 --> 00:03:48.886
Demi said.

53
00:03:48.906 --> 00:03:55.390
"You're always such a good little boy," Dan said in a nasty tone.

54
00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:58.332
"Why shouldn't we do it?"

55
00:03:59.624 --> 00:04:02.425
"I don't think my uncle Fritz would like it."

56
00:04:04.206 --> 00:04:06.507
"Did he ever forbid bullfights?"

57
00:04:06.988 --> 00:04:08.028
Dan demanded.

58
00:04:08.048 --> 00:04:12.590
"No, I don't think so," Demi admitted.

59
00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:19.073
"Then be quiet," Dan said as he pulled a red handkerchief from his pocket.

60
00:04:19.093 --> 00:04:23.095
"Here's a rag to wave at the cow, Tommy.

61
00:04:24.255 --> 00:04:25.476
I'll help you stir her up."

62
00:04:26.956 --> 00:04:31.019
Dan went over the pasture wall with the others following right behind.

63
00:04:33.881 --> 00:04:38.144
Even Demi sat atop the wall and watched the scene with great interest.

64
00:04:39.485 --> 00:04:43.608
Tommy rode toward Buttercup and tapped her with his fishing pole.

65
00:04:43.628 --> 00:04:48.071
"Moo!" cried the surprised animal.

66
00:04:48.091 --> 00:04:49.972
"That's it!"

67
00:04:50.313 --> 00:04:51.033
Dan called.

68
00:04:51.053 --> 00:04:53.195
"Come on, Nat and Jack!

69
00:04:53.495 --> 00:04:54.756
Tap her with your poles."

70
00:04:57.808 --> 00:05:03.791
Poor Buttercup trotted around the field, getting more confused and excited every moment.

71
00:05:05.612 --> 00:05:08.954
No matter which way she turned, there was a boy with a pole.

72
00:05:10.155 --> 00:05:14.537
All at once she leaped over the wall and ran out of sight down the road.

73
00:05:14.557 --> 00:05:17.439
"Catch her!"

74
00:05:17.699 --> 00:05:18.479
Dan shouted.

75
00:05:18.499 --> 00:05:21.221
"If anything happens to her, Mr.

76
00:05:21.281 --> 00:05:22.762
Bauer will send me away!"

77
00:05:24.683 --> 00:05:29.050
Buttercup may have been old, but she led the boys on a merry chase.

78
00:05:30.871 --> 00:05:34.134
At last they caught her in a neighbor's flower garden.

79
00:05:35.655 --> 00:05:42.201
Borrowing a rope, Dan led her home, followed by a group of solemn boys and the donkey.

80
00:05:42.221 --> 00:05:48.326
"Look, Dan, she's all wet and muddy, and she's limping!"

81
00:05:48.726 --> 00:05:49.367
Nat said.

82
00:05:49.387 --> 00:05:53.690
"You're in trouble now," Tommy added.

83
00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:56.877
"So are you," Dan said.

84
00:05:56.897 --> 00:06:04.801
"We all helped except for Demi," Jack said, "but he was the one who first mentioned bullfighting."

85
00:06:06.302 --> 00:06:08.243
"I told Dan not to do it!"

86
00:06:08.603 --> 00:06:09.664
Demi protested.

87
00:06:09.684 --> 00:06:16.567
"Well, I guess this is the end for me," Dan said, "but I don't care."

88
00:06:18.829 --> 00:06:23.051
When the professor saw Buttercup and heard the story, he said little.

89
00:06:25.964 --> 00:06:30.568
He sent the boys to their rooms, which gave them time to worry about their punishment.

90
00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:38.435
The longer Dan sat on his bed, the more he thought about the warmth and kindness he'd received

91
00:06:38.475 --> 00:06:41.838
here, and the hardship and neglect he'd felt elsewhere.

92
00:06:43.039 --> 00:06:45.741
But he knew the Bauers were finished with him.

93
00:06:45.761 --> 00:06:53.308
"I've lived on the streets before," he told himself defiantly, "and I can do it again!"

94
00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:56.381
So he was ready when Mr.

95
00:06:56.441 --> 00:06:58.443
Bauer finally knocked on his door.

96
00:07:02.106 --> 00:07:08.551
greatly disappointed us, especially because you're usually so kind to animals," the professor began.

97
00:07:09.932 --> 00:07:14.036
He went on, and the more he talked, the worse Dan felt.

98
00:07:14.056 --> 00:07:17.419
"Why doesn't he hurry up and throw me out?"

99
00:07:17.819 --> 00:07:19.881
Dan thought as he stared at the floor.

100
00:07:19.901 --> 00:07:27.504
"However," the professor concluded, "I'm giving you one more chance because Mrs.

101
00:07:27.584 --> 00:07:28.606
Bauer believes in you.

102
00:07:29.868 --> 00:07:30.789
Shall we try again?"

103
00:07:30.809 --> 00:07:37.899
Dan looked up in surprise at this unexpected kindness and blurted out, "Yes, please!"
